{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Constellations: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja49'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 49 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Atthakāmavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Wanting to Help </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>9. Nakkhattajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Constellations: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nakkhattaṁ paṭimānentaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Waiting for a constellation, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attho bālaṁ upaccagā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a fool lets the good pass them by. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Attho atthassa nakkhattaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The good is the constellation of the good; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁ karissanti tārakā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for what do the stars matter? </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Nakkhattajātakaṁ navamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
